# Kaduna State University (KASU) Mapping Project

## Project Overview

This academic GIS project involved creating a detailed map of Kaduna State University from scratch.

The project was one of my practical GIS assignments and involved working with satellite imagery, GPS coordinates, manual digitization, and field verification to represent features within the university campus.

## Input

The project started with an image of the Kaduna State University campus obtained from Google Earth.

![KASU Input Image](./KASU%20INPUT.jpg)

## Mapping Process

The mapping process involved:

1. Obtaining the study area image from Google Earth.
2. Collecting 4–6 GPS coordinates from different locations within the study area using a mobile GPS waypoint application.
3. Using the collected coordinates to support the spatial referencing of the study area.
4. Manually digitizing features within the university campus, including buildings, footpaths, roads, parcels of land, and trees.
5. Revisiting the site for ground-truthing and verification of mapped features.
6. Producing the final digital map.

## Output

The final output was a digitized map of Kaduna State University showing the spatial features identified within the study area.

![KASU Digitized Map](./KASU%20OUTPUT.jpg)

## Skills Demonstrated

- GIS mapping
- Manual digitization
- GPS coordinate collection
- Spatial referencing
- Ground-truthing
- Cartographic design
- Geospatial data management

## Project Significance

This project strengthened my practical understanding of how GIS can be used to transform a real-world study area into a digital spatial representation through data collection, digitization, and field verification.

